## Work history

Moved every skin-owned renderer, stylesheet, resource, font, motion rule, theme value, and authoring path out of `scorepeek-overlay-ui`. Each bundled skin is now an independently built Wasm crate and exhaustive package manifest. `skins/shared` is an optional generic implementation shortcut with no production skin registry, IDs, or theme values.

Upgraded the skin package and input contract to API v2. Manifests declare generic resources with media types and all widget defaults. The host only interprets `font/*` resources specially. Inputs expose `backend` and `monotonic_ms`; each skin owns native/browser scheduling and motion. Package discovery scans `skins/*/skin.toml`.

Removed the host built-in/default Cyan dependency, moved appearance controls to manifest properties, and migrated config schema v8 typed background/frame/fill fields into schema v9 skin properties. Existing generic properties take precedence. Adding a widget is unavailable when no skin is installed.

Added the generic `skins/shared/tools/compose-css.bash` authoring helper, updated the living API/design/architecture documentation, and removed superseded direct-renderer examples and tests.

